[0.486, "o", "  # pd-fleet.yml — Port Daddy's own fleet configuration\r\n  #\r\n  # Retooled 2026-05-20 (see docs/fleet/2026-05-20-retool.md).\r\n  #\r\n  # The Old Way (pre-2026-05-20):\r\n  #   Ships published findings to pub/sub channels. The operator never\r\n  #   read them. Findings died in SQLite rows no human opened.\r\n  #\r\n  # The New Way:\r\n  #   Ships write to GitHub — PR comments (one per ship per PR, edited\r\n  #   in place), issues (deduped by title), and draft PRs for proposed\r\n  #   work. Channels remain, but they are internal plumbing for\r\n  #   ship-to-ship chaining, not the operator surface.\r\n  #\r\n  # Implementation primitive: lib/fleet/github-output.ts. Ships call\r\n  # `postPRComment`, `openIssue`, `openDraftPR`, `closeIssue` instead\r\n  # of `pd pub`. Today the helper shells out to `gh` and inherits the\r\n  # operator's auth. When the Port Daddy GitHub App lands, the helper\r\n"]
